1️⃣ LeetCode #300 — Longest Increasing Subsequence

Medium ⭐

class Solution {
    public int lengthOfLIS(int[] nums) {
        int[] dp = new int[nums.length];

        int answer = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            dp[i] = 1;

            for (int j = 0; j < i; j++) {
                if (nums[j] < nums[i]) {
                    dp[i] = Math.max(dp[i], dp[j] + 1);
                }
            }

            answer = Math.max(answer, dp[i]);
        }

        return answer;
    }
}
🧠 Simple idea

dp[i] = nums[i]-la end aagura longest increasing subsequence length

Example:

[10, 9, 2, 5, 3, 7, 101, 18]

One LIS:

2 → 5 → 7 → 101

Answer = 4

Time: O(n²)
Space: O(n)

Interview follow-up-la O(n log n) solution ketka chance irukku; first indha DP version logic strong pannunga.

2️⃣ LeetCode #516 — Longest Palindromic Subsequence

Medium

class Solution {
    public int longestPalindromeSubseq(String s) {
        int n = s.length();

        int[] dp = new int[n];

        for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            dp[i] = 1;

            int diagonal = 0;

            for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
                int temp = dp[j];

                if (s.charAt(i) == s.charAt(j)) {
                    dp[j] = diagonal + 2;
                } else {
                    dp[j] = Math.max(dp[j], dp[j - 1]);
                }

                diagonal = temp;
            }
        }

        return dp[n - 1];
    }
}
🧠 Example
s = "bbbab"

Longest palindromic subsequence:

bbbb

Answer = 4

Core idea:

If:

s[i] == s[j]

then:

dp = inside palindrome + 2

Otherwise:

max(left, right)

Time: O(n²)
Space: O(n)

3️⃣ LeetCode #72 — Edit Distance

Hard ⭐⭐

class Solution {
    public int minDistance(String word1, String word2) {
        int m = word1.length();
        int n = word2.length();

        int[] dp = new int[n + 1];

        for (int j = 0; j <= n; j++) {
            dp[j] = j;
        }

        for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {
            int diagonal = dp[0];

            dp[0] = i;

            for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {
                int temp = dp[j];

                if (word1.charAt(i - 1) == word2.charAt(j - 1)) {
                    dp[j] = diagonal;
                } else {
                    dp[j] = 1 + Math.min(
                        diagonal,
                        Math.min(dp[j], dp[j - 1])
                    );
                }

                diagonal = temp;
            }
        }

        return dp[n];
    }
}
